{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":20954465,"ns":0,"title":"Flue-gas condensation","extract":"Flue-gas condensation is the process by which flue gas is cooled to below its water dew point, with the heat released by the resulting condensation of water being recovered as low-temperature heat.\nCooling of the flue gas can be performed with a heat exchanger or via a condensing scrubber.","description":"Process for heat recovery","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}